CloudBurrow patch 3 to github.com/goccy/bigquery-emulator v0.8.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1061; the bug: #1119).

The bug: a GEOGRAPHY a streamed row, a load or a query's rows gave as WKT
text was bound as that text and read back as it was given, POINT (3 4),
where BigQuery writes a geography with no space between a geometry's type
and its parenthesis, POINT(3 4), and an empty one as GEOMETRYCOLLECTION
EMPTY (every example in BigQuery's geography functions reference). The
patch writes such text so in Repository.AddTableData, which every write of
rows goes through; its numbers, GeoJSON, and a GEOGRAPHY inside a RECORD or
a REPEATED column are left as they are. The engine's own geographies are
written so by googlesqlite patch 12. internal/contentdata/geography_test.go
fails without the patch and passes with it.

